The notes implement $c=\bar a b+a\bar b$ with two inverters, two AND gates and an OR gate. This dataflow version keeps the internal gate signals and requires no additional component files.

```vhdl
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity xor2 is
    port (a, b : in BIT; c : out BIT);
end entity xor2;

architecture exm1 of xor2 is
    signal p, q, r, s : BIT;
begin
    p <= not a;
    q <= not b;
    r <= p and b;
    s <= a and q;
    c <= r or s;
end architecture exm1;

entity tb_xor2 is
end entity tb_xor2;

architecture io of tb_xor2 is
    signal u, v, w : BIT;
begin
    g1: entity WORK.xor2(exm1) port map (a=>u, b=>v, c=>w);
    u <= '0', '1' after 100 ns, '0' after 200 ns;
    v <= '0', '1' after 150 ns, '0' after 300 ns, '1' after 420 ns;

end architecture io;
```

**Timing diagram** (aligned intervals, widths not time-scaled):

```text
t (ns)       0      100    150    200    300    420
             │      │      │      │      │      │
a            _______|‾‾‾‾‾‾|‾‾‾‾‾‾|______|______|______
